530-- [__fflush](../../../core/libs/prx/libSceLibcInternal/Stream.cpp) (libSceLibcInternal, NID `E1iwBYkG3CM`) reuses the public `fflush` implementation (`fflush_nid_postfix`) rather than FreeBSD 11.4 libc's unlocked helper ([fflush.c](https://github.com/freebsd/freebsd-src/blob/8c639945a44588f6cfdddfb057bb5aad88735da0/lib/libc/stdio/fflush.c)): it acquires stream locks. A closed stream returns 0 without setting `errno`, as FreeBSD does for a stream with 0 flags, instead of the public `fflush` result of -1 with `EBADF`. Passing null flushes all open streams and returns 0 when all writes succeed or EOF on write error. Console behavior is unverified.
